		(render_cache "DRC'S MUST BE RUN ON THE GERBERS PRIOR TO BUILDING BOARDS\n\n1.) BOARD MATERIAL: (SEE STACKUP BELOW)\n		□ RF35		□ RO4003\n		□ FR-4		□ RO4350\n		□ 4000-13EP\n\n2.) BOARD STACKUP\n		□ COMPONENTS ON TOP SIDE ONLY	□ COMPONENTS ON BOTH SIDES\n		____	LAYERS\n		FINISHED OVERALL THICKNESS: \n		□ .031 +/- .005\n		□ .062 +/- .005\n		□ .093 +/- .005\n		□ .125 +/- .005\n\n3.) COPPER WEIGHT:\n		EXTERNAL LAYERS: (SEE STACKUP BELOW) OUNCE FINISHED	\n		INTERNAL LAYERS: (SEE STACKUP BELOW) OUNCE FINISHED\n4.) PLATING:\n		□ HOT AIR SOLDER LEVEL (HASL) EXPOSED AREAS WITH LEADED SOLDER\n		  FINISH 50uIN MIN - 200uIN MAX.\n		□ FINISH: AS PER IPC ENIG. SPECIFICATION 4522, 2-4 MICRO-INCHES\n		  IMMERSION GOLD OVER 120-240 MICRO-INCHES NICKEL\n		□ OMIKRON WHITE TIN DEPOSITION PROCESS OR ANDREW APPROVED EQUIVALENT\n		  TIN PLATING SHALL BE 200 TO 250 MICRO INCHES IN THICKNESS.\n		□ STANDARD SPEC.\n5.) DRILLING:\n		UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED, PLATE ALL HOLES THRU. \n		SEE HOLE CHART FOR FINISHED HOLE SIZES AND QUANTITY.\n6.) HOLE SIZE TOLERANCES SHALL BE: \n		(SEE HOLE CHART)\n7.) SOLDERMASK:\n		□ TOP SIDE\n		□ BOTTOM SIDE\n		□ LIQUID PHOTO-IMAGEABLE SOLDERMASK SHALL BE APPLIED\n		  OVER BARE COPPER UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED\n		□ GREEN\n		□ BLUE\n		□ RED\n		□ BLACK\n		□ MATTE BLACK\n8.) SILKSCREEN:\n		□ TOP SIDE\n		□ BOTTOM SIDE\n		□ CHARACTER LEGEND TO BE SCREENED USING NON-CONDUCTIVE\n		  EPOXY BASED INK.\n		□ WHITE\n		□ ________________\n\n9.) BOW AND TWIST: MAXIMUM ACCEPTABLE IS 0.75% (IPC-TM-650)\n\n10.) FABRICATE IN ACCORDANCE WITH IPC-6011/6012, CLASS 2 (LATEST REVISIONS)\n\n11.) ACCEPTABILITY TO IPC-A-600 (LATEST REVISIONS)\n\n12.) CONDUCTOR INFORMATION:\n		DRC MUST BE RUN ON GERBERS BEFORE BUILDING BOARDS UNLESS\n		APPROVAL IS GIVEN IN WRITING. \n		SMALLEST TRACE:    _______\n		SMALLEST SPACING: _______\n		CONDUCTOR WIDTHS AND SPACING SHALL BE WITHIN +/-20% OF ARTWORK ORIGINALS.\n		CONTROLLED IMPEDANCE REQUIREMENTS AS CALLED OUT IN CONTROLLED IMPEDANCE NOTES.\n13.) REMOVE ALL BURRS AND BREAK SHARP EDGES 0.015 INCHES MAX\n14.) VENDOR INFORMATION:\n		VENDOR WILL PUT THEIR UL LOGO AND DATE CODE IN SILKSCREEN\n		ON THE COMPONENT SIDE IN THE UNOBSTRUCTED AREA\n15.) ALL 0.300mm VIA-IN-PAD SHALL BE PLATED, FILLED, AND FLATTENED."
